"mmorpg.word.press_alt_for_item_description": "[Alt] — item description",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.gem": "A gem for gear sockets.\nHow to use: drag it onto a piece of gear in your inventory — it fills one empty socket.\nThe gear needs a free socket and must not already have a gem of the same type.\nUpgrading: use 3 identical gems at once — the chance is listed on the gem.\nOn success you get the next rank gem, on failure all 3 gems are destroyed.\nThe highest rank gem cannot be upgraded.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.rune": "A rune for the Runeword Station.\nIt does nothing on its own.\nThe station has 6 rune slots: put in an item and the runes whose set exactly matches a runeword recipe.\nRunes drop from mobs and rewards, their value depends on the rune type.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.ingredient": "A profession ingredient.\nIt goes into the crafting grid (6 slots, 3x2) together with the profession tool.\nThe ingredient's stats are transferred to the result, so the higher its tier, the stronger the outcome.\nEvery ingredient has its own list of professions — other professions reject it.\nSome ingredients affect adjacent grid slots: read their own description (Alt).\nOnly one \"artifact\" ingredient (marked \"Only one of\") can be used per craft.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.smelted_essence": "Smelted essence.\nMade by smelting purified essence (dust) in a furnace or at a station.\nA profession material: used for condensed essence and gear recipes.\nIts tier matches the tier of the source dust.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.condensed_essence": "Condensed essence.\nCrafted from 3 smelted essences of the same tier.\nA profession material: used in upgrade and currency recipes.\nIts tier decides which recipes it fits.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.mining_stone": "A mystical stone.\nSometimes appears when mining ore.\nA profession material: used to craft tools and gear.\nIts tier depends on the ore that was mined.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.salvage_dust": "Purified essence.\nRepair: pick the essence up with the cursor and click damaged gear in your inventory.\nRestores the durability listed in the tooltip; if the gear tier is higher than the essence tier, the repair is 5 times weaker.\nA profession material: it is smelted into essence and used for scroll paper.\n4 essences of a lower tier combine into 1 essence of the next tier.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.craft_tool": "A profession tool.\nRight click to open this profession's crafting menu.\nPut ingredients into the grid; gear professions also require a matching piece of gear.\nThe tool is not consumed.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.backpack": "An adventurer's backpack.\nRight click to open its inventory.\nUpgrades are installed by dragging them onto the backpack.\nItems picked up by upgrades go straight inside.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.material_pouch": "A pouch for profession materials.\nRight click to open.\nIt stores ingredients, essences and stones.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.backpack_upgrade": "A backpack upgrade.\nDrag it onto a backpack in your inventory to install it.\nEach upgrade is installed once and works permanently.\nThe upgrade tier decides which backpack it fits.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.stat_soul": "A gear soul.\nIt holds a statted gear blueprint.\nHow to use: drag the soul onto empty gear.\nThe soul type must match the gear slot (if a slot is specified).\nA soul with gear inside can be identified with an Identify Tome.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.crafted_consumable": "A profession crafting result.\nIts stats depend on the ingredients used.\nFood lasts long, potions are stronger but shorter, scrolls buff nearby allies.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.alchemy_potion": "An alchemy potion.\nRight click to drink: restores health or mana depending on the type.\nThe restore amount is a percentage of your maximum.\nIt is brewed from ingredients, so its power depends on them.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.currency": "Gear currency.\nHow to use: drag it onto a piece of gear in your inventory.\nShift shows requirements, instability and the chance to break the item.\nEvery use adds instability; when the bar is full the item can no longer be modified.\nPurification orbs reduce instability.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.loot_crate": "A reward crate.\nRight click to open and take the contents.\nThe crate tier decides the reward level.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.tiered": "A profession and crafting material.\nUsed in gear, tool and currency recipes.\nThe item tier affects the result's power.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.block": "A mod block.\nPlace it in the world and right click it to use.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.common_soul_produce": "Right click to create a common gear soul.\nThe soul gets the tier of your level and fits any slot.\nConsumes 1 item.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.identify_tome": "Right click to identify gear souls in your inventory.\nEvery soul without stats becomes a ready piece of gear.\nOne tome is spent per soul.\nSouls that already have stats are left alone.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.loot_crate.default": "A reward crate.\nRight click to open.\nThe contents depend on the crate tier.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.source_of_strength": "A crafting material.\nNeeded to craft upgrade stones, for example the magic upgrade stone (9 pcs).\nObtained by salvaging rarity essences.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.projectile.fireball": "A service projectile of the fire school.\nNever given to players — a spell summons it on cast.\nDamage and speed come from the spell, not from the item.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.projectile.snowball": "A service projectile of the water school.\nNever given to players — a spell summons it on cast.\nDamage and speed come from the spell, not from the item.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.projectile.slimeball": "A service projectile of the nature school.\nNever given to players — a spell summons it on cast.\nDamage and speed come from the spell, not from the item.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.scroll.paper": "An inscription material.\nUsed to craft scrolls together with the scribe's tool.\nCrafted from paper, string and two tier 1 purified essences.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.misc.teleport_back": "Right click and hold to return to the entrance.\nOnly works inside dungeons and maps, useless in the normal world.\nSingle use.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.loot_table_chest": "Right click to open a reward chest.\nThe contents come from the loot table attached to the item.\nSingle use.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.full_favor": "Right click to gain 1000 favor.\nFavor is spent on NPC services and goods.\nMade from an empty vessel of favor.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.empty_favor": "Right click to fill the vessel.\nTakes 1000 favor and turns into a full vessel.\nRequires level 20 and at least 1000 favor.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.custom_crate": "A crate with gear of a chosen rarity.\nRight click to open.\nThe crate itself sets the rarity and tier.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.newbie_gear_bag": "Right click to get a starter gear set.\nThe set is picked for your chosen class.\nGiven to new players on their first join.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.salvage_hammer": "A salvaging tool.\nPick the hammer up with the cursor and click a piece of gear in your inventory to salvage it into essence.\nThe hammer is not consumed.\nIt does not salvage named or enchanted items.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.socket_extractor": "A gem extractor.\nPick it up with the cursor and click socketed gear — the first gem returns to your inventory.\nThe socket is freed and the extractor is not consumed.\nThe item must have at least one socketed gem.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.mat.infused_iron": "A currency crafting material.\nUsed in the Orb of Chaos recipe, which rerolls all affixes.\nAlso counts as a profession material.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.mat.crystallized_essence": "A currency crafting material.\nUsed in the Orb of Blessing and Orb of Turbulence recipes.\nAlso counts as a profession material.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.mat.golden_orb": "A currency crafting material.\nNeeded for the Leaf of Change, Orb of Unique Blessing, Orb of Corruption and Orb of Infinity.\nAlso counts as a profession material.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.mat.mythic_essence": "A currency crafting material.\nNeeded for the Orb of Corruption and Orb of Infinity.\nAlso counts as a profession material.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.potions.reset_all_perks": "Right click to drink: resets all talents.\nSpent talent points are refunded.\nLeaves an empty bottle.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.potions.add_reset_perk_points": "Right click to drink: +5 talent reset points.\nA reset point removes one talent without losing the rest.\nLeaves an empty bottle.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.potions.reset_spells": "Right click to drink: resets all learned spells.\nFrees up your spell slots.\nLeaves an empty bottle.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.potions.reset_stats": "Right click to drink: resets your allocated stat points.\nThe points are refunded.\nLeaves an empty bottle.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.potions.death_potion": "Right click to drink... and find out.\nKills whoever drinks it. Not recommended in hardcore.\nIt is a joke, not a medicine.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.backpack.normal": "An adventurer's backpack.\nRight click to open its inventory.\nUpgrades (auto pickup, auto salvage) are installed by dragging them onto the backpack.\nItems picked up by upgrades go straight inside.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.backpack.material_pouch": "A pouch for profession materials.\nRight click to open.\nIt stores ingredients, essences and stones.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.teleporter": "A teleporter block.\nPlace it and right click to open the adventure map.\nIt is used to pick a map and travel into a dungeon.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.runeword_station": "The Runeword Station.\nPlace the block and right click it.\nPut in an item and the complete rune set from a recipe — the item gains that runeword.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.portal": "A portal into an adventure.\nCreated by the game when entering a map or dungeon.\nStepping into it takes you to the chosen adventure.\nNormally not placed by hand.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.rarity.essence.base": "A rarity essence.\nRight click to combine 9 such essences into a rarity upgrade stone.\nCan be salvaged with a hammer into Source of Strength.\nThe essence rarity decides which gear rarity the stone works on.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.rarity.upgrade_stone.base": "A rarity upgrade stone.\nHow to use: drag it onto a piece of gear in your inventory.\nRaises the item rarity by one step.\nRequirement: the item's upgrade level must be at least the value listed on the stone.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.dungeon_key": "An Infinite Dungeons key.\nRight click to pick a dungeon and difficulty, then press Start.\nThe dungeon is built above you: you need open sky and a dimension without a ceiling.\nThe key is consumed on start.\nDrops rarely from hostile mobs.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.dungeon_coin": "An Infinite Dungeons coin.\nThe dungeon shop currency: after clearing a dungeon, right click the trader villager.\nCoins buy reward crates and gear.\nEach shop takes its own coin: skeletal is the lowest tier, nether the middle one, void the highest.\nDrops from mobs inside dungeons.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.infinite_dungeons.reward_crate": "An Infinite Dungeons reward crate.\nRight click to open: it gives one random reward from its own list.\nThe name tells you what is inside, some crates can hit a jackpot.\nBought in the dungeon shop for coins.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.divine_missions.mission": "A god's mission.\nRight click to hand in the items the mission asks for; once everything is collected it completes and pays out.\nThe mission has a time limit: if you run out, it disappears.\nMissions are given at the shrine.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.divine_missions.shrine": "A god's shrine.\nPlace the block and right click it to open the mission menu.\nThis is where you take missions and track them.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.family.gear": "Gear.\nWorn in its own slot: helmet, chestplate, leggings, boots, weapon, ring or amulet.\nStats are generated on drop: the higher the tier and rarity, the more and the stronger they are.\nThe tooltip lists the level and stat requirements together with whether you meet them.\nDurability is repaired with purified essence, the item is salvaged with a salvage hammer, and currency changes its rarity and sockets.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.ingredient.wishing_bowl": "The Wishing Bowl is an artifact ingredient.\nProfessions: jewel crafting, armor crafting.\nIt raises the minimum rarity of the crafted gear by 1.\nArtifact: only one such ingredient per craft.\nIt does not affect neighbouring slots.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.ingredient.enigma_stone": "The Enigma Stone is a positional ingredient.\nProfessions: jewel crafting, weapon crafting, alchemy.\nIt adds spell critical damage and spell critical chance (the range is shown in the tooltip).\nIngredients touching it on a side lose 25% effectiveness — place it in a corner of the 3x2 grid.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.ingredient.blackpearl": "The Black Pearl is a positional ingredient.\nProfessions: jewel crafting, alchemy.\nIt adds critical damage to the item.\nIngredients touching it on a side lose 20% effectiveness — place it in a corner of the 3x2 grid.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.ingredient.bone_figurine": "The Bone Figurine works through its position in the crafting grid, not on its own.\nProfessions: jewel crafting, armor crafting, weapon crafting.\nIngredients that do NOT touch it get +10% effectiveness.\nIngredients touching it on a side (up, down, left, right) get -25% effectiveness.\nThe grid is 3x2: in a corner the figurine touches only two slots, so place it in a corner and keep your strong ingredients away from it.\nThe figurine itself gives the item no stats — only this neighbour effect.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.ingredient.endergem": "Endergem is an artifact positional ingredient.\nProfessions: all of them (jewel crafting, armor crafting, weapon crafting, alchemy, cooking, inscription).\nIt adds 2 random stats and raises the minimum rarity of the result.\nDownsides: crafting success chance -25%, ingredients touching it lose 20% effectiveness.\nArtifact: only one such ingredient per craft.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.ingredient.pot_of_greed": "The Pot of Greed is an artifact ingredient.\nProfessions: alchemy, cooking, inscription.\nIt grants +2 to the maximum uses of the crafted consumable (food, potion, scroll).\nArtifact: only one such ingredient per craft.\nIt does not affect neighbouring slots.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.ingredient.soul_matrix": "The Soul Matrix is an artifact ingredient.\nProfessions: all six.\nIt raises the crafting success chance by 20% — handy together with ingredients that lower it.\nArtifact: only one such ingredient per craft.\nIt does not affect neighbouring slots.",
"mmorpg.item.desc.ingredient.rock_jade": "Rock Jade is an artifact positional ingredient.\nProfessions: all of them (jewel crafting, armor crafting, weapon crafting, alchemy, cooking, inscription).\nIt adds a random stat and raises the minimum rarity of the result.\nDownsides: crafting success chance -10%, and ingredients touching it lose 20% effectiveness.\nBecause of \"Only one of\", you cannot add a second artifact to the same craft.",
"key.mmorpg.hold_open_wiki": "Hold on item: open in Epoch Wiki",
